WEBVTT

00:27.083 --> 00:28.416
Kotaro. Are you okay?

00:29.000 --> 00:30.250
Can you drink some water?

00:33.333 --> 00:35.625
-Miss Futaba?
-Yes?

00:36.750 --> 00:40.083
Am I going to die?

00:41.708 --> 00:42.916
Don't worry.

00:43.541 --> 00:46.458
My mother is praying to the gods.

01:06.125 --> 01:10.708
One, two, three, four.

01:11.375 --> 01:15.750
One, two, three, four.

01:16.250 --> 01:21.666
One, two, three, four.

01:24.541 --> 01:25.541
Futaba?

01:26.750 --> 01:28.041
What's the matter?

01:33.458 --> 01:34.666
Mother.

01:36.833 --> 01:40.333
Will cholera really ever end?

01:42.125 --> 01:43.916
Father is already gone,

01:44.000 --> 01:46.708
and the people in town keep dying.

01:49.833 --> 01:54.000
And yet, we're still praying to the gods.

01:55.250 --> 01:56.083
Futaba.

01:57.500 --> 02:00.958
Everything that happens in this world
is arranged by the gods.

02:01.041 --> 02:05.750
That is why all we can do is pray.

02:09.083 --> 02:11.208
As long as we keep praying,

02:11.708 --> 02:15.875
the gods will protect us
from any war or plague.

02:17.625 --> 02:19.083
Let us have faith.

02:24.416 --> 02:26.583
Shall we prepare dinner?

02:28.583 --> 02:29.500
Okay.

02:48.291 --> 02:49.375
Mother?

02:50.041 --> 02:54.083
Mother!

02:55.166 --> 02:58.750
Mother!

03:39.666 --> 03:42.208
What's wrong, Kokushu?

03:48.458 --> 03:50.291
It's not you I want!

03:50.375 --> 03:51.666
Let's go!

04:00.458 --> 04:01.500
Over here!

04:13.625 --> 04:15.208
Go, Futaba! Go!

04:18.083 --> 04:19.375
Go!

04:47.583 --> 04:48.666
Draw your sword.

04:49.750 --> 04:51.833
You're done babysitting, right?

04:59.250 --> 05:00.458
Oh, come on.

05:01.583 --> 05:04.166
Are you bullshitting me?

05:10.458 --> 05:14.125
Have you turned into a gutless bastard,
Kokushu the Manslayer?

05:22.416 --> 05:24.333
How have you been living since then?

05:34.958 --> 05:37.375
Those government bastards are selfish.

05:38.333 --> 05:40.625
They told us to fight and kill.

05:41.125 --> 05:44.541
But when they no longer need us,
they tell us to abandon our swords.

05:45.208 --> 05:49.541
That's why I'm grateful to the one
who came up with this game.

05:51.500 --> 05:54.500
I can go back to the way I was back then.

05:57.166 --> 05:59.833
We shouldn't hesitate to do so.

06:01.541 --> 06:02.375
Come on.

06:04.500 --> 06:06.000
Draw your sword!

06:32.416 --> 06:33.958
Much better.

06:34.625 --> 06:37.625
There's Kokushu the Manslayer.

06:59.416 --> 07:01.583
What's wrong, Kokushu?

07:29.125 --> 07:30.458
That's better.

07:53.000 --> 07:54.833
What the hell are you doing?

08:03.250 --> 08:04.583
Shujiro!

08:14.000 --> 08:16.750
We're not done yet!

08:48.333 --> 08:50.291
Sir Saga, what happened to you?

08:52.458 --> 08:54.666
Come, get inside.

09:06.541 --> 09:08.583
Please rest.

09:08.666 --> 09:10.333
Thank you for helping us.

09:10.416 --> 09:12.583
Not at all. Let me know whatever you need.

09:13.166 --> 09:17.875
What you have done for me
is much more than I could ever repay.

09:20.125 --> 09:21.500
That was a long time ago.

09:25.666 --> 09:27.250
Well, then. I'll excuse myself.

09:40.458 --> 09:42.666
Still sharp.

09:50.416 --> 09:52.166
You saved me back there.

09:52.916 --> 09:53.791
Thank you.

09:54.791 --> 09:58.541
Thank you for saving me as well.

10:00.291 --> 10:03.583
I'll take you as far as
the Tokaido Road in the morning.

10:04.083 --> 10:06.375
You take your wooden tag off and run.

10:10.750 --> 10:11.875
It's against the rules.

10:14.000 --> 10:16.333
Your life is more important than rules.

10:17.416 --> 10:18.375
I won't stop.

10:18.458 --> 10:19.750
Don't you get it?

10:21.625 --> 10:22.875
A child cannot survive.

10:22.958 --> 10:24.500
But I can't afford to run away.

10:27.083 --> 10:31.625
If I run, there are lives I cannot save.

10:38.625 --> 10:39.625
Cholera?

10:50.583 --> 10:51.625
Who's there?

10:51.708 --> 10:55.583
Calm down.
I have no intention of fighting you.

10:57.208 --> 10:58.708
Why are you here?

10:58.791 --> 11:01.333
Why don't we talk face-to-face?

11:02.583 --> 11:05.875
I'll enter with my hands up,
so don't start slashing at me, okay?

11:11.916 --> 11:13.375
Did you miss me?

11:14.833 --> 11:16.333
What do you want?

11:16.416 --> 11:18.166
Put your sword down first, will you?

11:20.291 --> 11:23.125
If I wanted to kill you,
I wouldn't come through the front.

11:23.208 --> 11:24.333
Come on. You too, miss.

11:31.208 --> 11:34.625
You're so stubborn, Kokushu the Manslayer.

11:36.708 --> 11:38.791
How do you know that name?

11:38.875 --> 11:41.041
Never mind how I know.

11:41.125 --> 11:44.708
What's more important
is why I came here, isn't it?

11:47.166 --> 11:51.666
You see, I'm here with
an incredibly good deal for you today.

11:52.541 --> 11:53.625
What is it?

11:57.166 --> 11:59.583
I want you to form an alliance with me.

12:02.000 --> 12:03.125
An alliance?

12:04.166 --> 12:05.750
What's your intention?

12:07.541 --> 12:11.708
Don't you think this "Kodoku" game
seems rather suspicious?

12:15.833 --> 12:18.875
What do they gain by making
skilled fighters kill each other?

12:19.500 --> 12:21.583
Why do they make us travel to Tokyo?

12:22.958 --> 12:26.708
Do they really intend
to reward someone with 100,000 yen?

12:28.416 --> 12:30.250
Who is behind it all?

12:30.750 --> 12:33.041
I'm sure you are curious too.

12:40.833 --> 12:43.333
The other participants
said that the government officials

12:43.416 --> 12:45.916
might be using it as a way
to seize the swords.

12:46.000 --> 12:48.708
If that was all,
they could have killed us at the temple.

12:48.791 --> 12:50.875
They wouldn't need
to bother with all this.

12:51.791 --> 12:52.708
That's true.

12:53.208 --> 12:55.625
I heard that the survivors
of the old shogunate forces

12:55.708 --> 12:58.708
are gathering skilled warriors
for revenge.

12:59.250 --> 13:01.083
There's also a rumor that foreigners

13:01.166 --> 13:04.000
are trying to incite a civil war
to crush Japan.

13:04.083 --> 13:06.666
But none of these rumors
have been verified.

13:08.416 --> 13:11.583
We don't know
what the organizer is scheming.

13:12.958 --> 13:16.708
Or what they'll be launching
at us going forward.

13:17.208 --> 13:18.916
What we do know

13:20.208 --> 13:23.125
is that whoever's pulling the strings
has serious power.

13:24.416 --> 13:25.791
That's why joining forces

13:25.875 --> 13:28.833
would enable us
to gather more information.

13:28.916 --> 13:31.375
If we can find out who they are,

13:31.458 --> 13:34.041
we'll get closer to the 100,000 yen.

13:36.708 --> 13:41.291
So? Feel a little more like listening now?

13:47.250 --> 13:50.083
Will this mess be taken care of?
I hope there's no problem.

13:51.208 --> 13:54.791
It'll be back to normal by morning.
No one will notice anything.

13:54.875 --> 13:56.916
And? How many are there remaining?

13:57.416 --> 14:01.416
One hundred and twenty-eight participants
have passed through the gate.

14:02.958 --> 14:04.750
That's more than I had estimated.

14:05.791 --> 14:08.916
True to form, the samurai
are stubborn to the last breath.

14:09.000 --> 14:12.250
Still, the stench of blood
is overwhelming, don't you think?

14:13.750 --> 14:17.416
The organizer will join you all later.

14:17.916 --> 14:22.208
Until then, please relax
and enjoy the estate at your leisure.

14:32.083 --> 14:33.583
After leaving Tenryuji Temple,

14:33.666 --> 14:38.041
we pass through Seki in Ise Province,
Chiryu, Hamamatsu, Shimada,

14:38.125 --> 14:40.083
Hakone, and Shinagawa.

14:40.833 --> 14:43.708
I calculated the number
of wooden tags needed to pass

14:43.791 --> 14:45.416
against the number of participants.

14:46.083 --> 14:49.666
There are 292 participants.

14:50.458 --> 14:51.958
And the number of tags required

14:52.041 --> 14:56.000
to pass the final checkpoint,
Shinagawa, is 30.

14:56.583 --> 14:57.708
Which means?

15:02.416 --> 15:06.666
It's possible for more than one person
to reach Tokyo.

15:07.375 --> 15:08.833
That's right.

15:09.375 --> 15:12.208
A maximum of nine people can reach Tokyo.

15:14.375 --> 15:17.958
The 100,000 yen may be divided
among those nine people,

15:18.041 --> 15:21.166
or perhaps they will be
ordered to do something more.

15:21.250 --> 15:23.458
We don't know the organizer's goal.

15:23.541 --> 15:26.291
That being said,
if nine people can make it to the end,

15:26.375 --> 15:29.708
there's no issue with the three of us
teaming up and heading for Tokyo.

15:30.375 --> 15:32.708
So? Not a bad idea, is it?

15:37.041 --> 15:39.000
Why us?

15:41.541 --> 15:44.750
You are different
from the other participants.

15:47.208 --> 15:49.500
Besides, as long as
this little miss is with you,

15:49.583 --> 15:52.333
you won't betray me, will you?

15:53.500 --> 15:57.333
You mean that if I betray you,
you intend to kill her?

15:58.750 --> 15:59.875
That's correct.

16:00.625 --> 16:03.041
She's a hostage, so to speak.

16:04.958 --> 16:09.750
Although, a time may come
when you'll have to kill this little miss.

16:15.375 --> 16:16.916
Well, take your time.

16:17.416 --> 16:20.666
There's an inn called Uzuya in Yokkaichi.

16:21.250 --> 16:25.208
If you're willing to form an alliance,
come to that inn on the third evening.

16:28.250 --> 16:29.333
Oh.

16:29.416 --> 16:31.458
One piece of advice.

16:33.333 --> 16:37.375
It's not that you cannot kill.
You simply choose not to.

16:39.500 --> 16:42.000
A manslayer is a manslayer for life.

16:43.083 --> 16:47.291
You are still a killer, Kokushu Saga.

16:50.375 --> 16:51.333
I'll see you again.

16:52.083 --> 16:52.916
Wait.

16:54.541 --> 16:55.916
Tell me one thing.

16:57.958 --> 17:00.291
Why did you join Kodoku?

17:02.791 --> 17:05.791
Well, I wonder.

17:08.416 --> 17:11.208
Maybe I just wanted to see it for myself.

17:13.250 --> 17:15.458
The end of the samurai.

17:19.625 --> 17:21.291
I'll be expecting good news.

17:29.291 --> 17:30.666
Get some rest.

17:47.250 --> 17:50.833
Mother. Have some water.

17:58.708 --> 17:59.833
Futaba…

18:01.041 --> 18:02.833
I'm sorry.

18:07.000 --> 18:09.416
I'll take care of everything.

18:13.250 --> 18:14.416
Please.

18:14.500 --> 18:15.958
Please.

18:16.541 --> 18:18.666
Please. I only need a little.

18:18.750 --> 18:20.375
Please save the children.

18:20.458 --> 18:23.583
No one in this town has any money left.

18:27.750 --> 18:30.833
No one's gonna believe this stuff, right?

18:30.916 --> 18:31.833
No chance.

18:31.916 --> 18:33.625
What's this? You want money?

18:33.708 --> 18:34.666
Yes.

18:34.750 --> 18:35.583
Take it.

18:36.083 --> 18:38.125
I can't deal with this crap.

18:40.250 --> 18:45.708
HOKOKU NEWSPAPER
PARTICIPANTS WANTED

18:49.416 --> 18:51.791
You! Begging is prohibited.

18:52.708 --> 18:53.541
Hey!

18:57.458 --> 18:59.250
Miss Futaba.

19:00.083 --> 19:01.458
I feel sick.

19:02.541 --> 19:03.625
It'll be okay.

19:04.500 --> 19:06.958
The gods are protecting you.

19:08.250 --> 19:09.583
Keep fighting.

19:11.791 --> 19:14.666
Kotaro?

19:15.791 --> 19:16.625
Kotaro!

23:07.833 --> 23:08.708
A ritual dance?

23:13.708 --> 23:14.583
Yes.

23:16.041 --> 23:17.541
What were you praying for?

23:22.416 --> 23:24.500
For everyone to fulfill their lives

23:25.833 --> 23:28.583
and ascend happily to heaven.

23:34.500 --> 23:36.125
My mother taught me.

23:38.416 --> 23:43.416
She took care of children
who had lost their parents.

23:45.291 --> 23:46.500
But now,

23:47.375 --> 23:49.875
she is bedridden with cholera.

23:52.500 --> 23:54.458
The villagers left behind

23:55.166 --> 23:57.666
are also suffering
from cholera and poverty.

24:03.625 --> 24:05.000
Shujiro.

24:07.000 --> 24:09.041
I need money.

24:11.166 --> 24:12.750
But I'm weak.

24:14.083 --> 24:15.958
I cannot stay alive by myself.

24:20.833 --> 24:22.291
So I'm begging you.

24:24.333 --> 24:26.500
Will you please take me with you?

24:30.708 --> 24:32.375
I'll do whatever it takes.

24:32.875 --> 24:34.458
Even if later it means…

24:36.416 --> 24:40.166
you have no choice but to kill me.

24:41.958 --> 24:45.083
I want to do everything I can
until the very end.

24:47.500 --> 24:50.958
Please, I beg of you.

25:04.833 --> 25:07.208
I also have family I want to save.

25:12.708 --> 25:15.791
We will survive this, Futaba.

25:23.166 --> 25:24.083
Yes.

25:37.833 --> 25:39.166
I appreciate your help.

25:40.083 --> 25:42.583
Here. Take these with you.

25:45.791 --> 25:50.416
That sword of yours
carved a way into a new era.

25:51.458 --> 25:54.750
Thanks to you, townsfolk like us
have been able to live in peace.

25:55.791 --> 25:57.375
I can't thank you enough for that.

25:58.625 --> 26:00.541
But the times have changed.

26:04.250 --> 26:05.083
Please.

26:10.833 --> 26:12.083
Thank you for everything.

26:12.583 --> 26:14.666
I wish you both luck with your swords.

26:27.250 --> 26:31.833
HOME MINISTRY, TOKYO

26:38.916 --> 26:39.750
Enter.

26:45.208 --> 26:47.625
Sorry for keeping you waiting.

26:47.708 --> 26:49.708
Kawaji. Take a seat.

26:51.208 --> 26:53.625
Home Minister.
What is this matter of concern?

26:54.791 --> 26:55.875
Here.

26:56.375 --> 26:58.083
HOKOKU NEWSPAPER
PARTICIPANTS WANTED

26:58.166 --> 27:01.291
We seized this in Tokyo recently.

27:02.083 --> 27:03.916
I'm aware of this.

27:04.416 --> 27:07.875
I was going to investigate it
a little more before reporting it to you.

27:07.958 --> 27:10.541
One hundred thousand yen
is an enormous sum of money.

27:10.625 --> 27:11.458
Yes.

27:12.041 --> 27:14.166
Last night, we confirmed

27:14.250 --> 27:17.750
many shizoku wielding weapons
had assembled at Tenryuji Temple in Kyoto.

27:18.250 --> 27:22.208
We're still unable to get in touch with
Jinbe Ando, who infiltrated the event.

27:22.291 --> 27:24.541
Are the shizoku scheming a rebellion?

27:24.625 --> 27:26.875
We don't know their goal yet.

27:27.375 --> 27:30.500
However, the shizoku,
doomed remnants of the samurai,

27:30.583 --> 27:32.625
have started something in Kyoto.

27:32.708 --> 27:35.875
Behind them is someone
with enough financial power

27:35.958 --> 27:39.041
to distribute a fake newspaper
throughout the country.

27:39.666 --> 27:41.333
Those are the facts.

27:42.041 --> 27:43.375
We don't know what may happen

27:43.458 --> 27:46.958
if funds gather under the shizoku
dissatisfied with the new government.

27:47.041 --> 27:49.250
We must launch
an investigation immediately.

27:49.333 --> 27:52.875
Maejima, the shizoku are like
tigers without fangs now.

27:52.958 --> 27:56.083
-We need not be afraid--
-We must not underestimate them.

27:56.166 --> 27:59.708
Just how much damage do you think
we suffered in the civil war last year?

28:01.250 --> 28:03.875
Our nation has just been reborn.

28:04.875 --> 28:06.875
Should there be another civil war now,

28:06.958 --> 28:09.000
it will diminish our nation's strength,

28:09.083 --> 28:11.125
and we will be swallowed by the West.

28:12.625 --> 28:13.541
Kawaji.

28:14.041 --> 28:16.125
Contact the Police Bureau to investigate.

28:16.208 --> 28:19.916
Find out who is behind this
and what their purpose is.

28:20.500 --> 28:22.791
-I want every detail.
-Yes, sir.

28:36.958 --> 28:38.750
Didn't you hear me?

28:39.291 --> 28:43.666
I asked if you saw a samurai
with a little brat passing this way.

28:46.000 --> 28:47.291
Useless.

28:48.083 --> 28:50.666
Please, have mercy. I beg you!

28:51.166 --> 28:52.791
Have mercy.

28:52.875 --> 28:54.333
Brute!

28:54.416 --> 28:56.250
Don't attack non-participants.

29:01.666 --> 29:03.625
Who the hell are you?

29:03.708 --> 29:05.375
Ukyo Kikuomi.

29:05.875 --> 29:07.000
Yeah?

29:07.083 --> 29:10.291
So you're the famous
Guardian God of the Court Nobles.

29:10.916 --> 29:12.291
Hurry and leave now.

29:13.583 --> 29:15.250
I've heard rumors about you.

29:15.333 --> 29:16.958
What a pitiful creature.

29:17.458 --> 29:21.291
Serving your master so well
only to get ditched so easily.

29:24.375 --> 29:27.333
That means you and I are the same.

29:27.416 --> 29:28.375
Silence.

29:29.208 --> 29:31.708
Don't count me
among the vile breed you belong to.

29:35.916 --> 29:37.250
Let's play.

30:47.500 --> 30:50.750
Enough of your squirming about,
you twitchy bastard.

30:51.333 --> 30:53.416
What's wrong? Is that all you can do?

31:12.291 --> 31:14.083
Are we done here?

31:14.666 --> 31:19.458
I don't have the time
to fight someone like you.

31:27.833 --> 31:30.583
Mr. Ukyo! You cannot see Lord Kazanin!

31:33.125 --> 31:34.291
Mr. Ukyo!

31:36.500 --> 31:38.041
Lord Kazanin.

31:38.125 --> 31:41.041
What do you mean
by abandoning the Kikuomi family?

31:41.125 --> 31:42.416
I'm eating.

31:45.458 --> 31:47.625
We, the Kikuomi family,

31:48.125 --> 31:50.750
have risked our lives many times
to save you court nobles.

31:51.875 --> 31:53.875
This is how you repay us?

31:54.916 --> 31:59.041
The samurai who have been stripped
of their swords have no use now.

32:02.000 --> 32:04.791
The government took away
your property too, didn't they?

32:04.875 --> 32:09.041
If you bow your head,
I might consider hiring you as my servant.

32:11.666 --> 32:12.708
You insolent bastard.

32:12.791 --> 32:13.833
Don't move!

32:15.125 --> 32:16.125
Put your hands down!

32:22.875 --> 32:24.333
Hurry up and take him away!

32:25.166 --> 32:26.583
Don't touch me!

32:28.625 --> 32:30.166
I'll leave on my own.

32:34.458 --> 32:36.458
He should know his place.

32:43.416 --> 32:46.750
My Lord, we cannot go on any longer.

32:48.083 --> 32:50.416
We have sold off everything we can.

32:51.666 --> 32:55.333
All we have left… is this.

32:57.875 --> 32:59.791
We've been deprived
of our purpose to live.

33:00.375 --> 33:03.833
Now our country
asks us to sell our pride as well?

33:06.791 --> 33:08.708
We have endured long enough.

33:11.708 --> 33:13.500
In order to protect our honor,

33:15.416 --> 33:17.458
we have no choice but to commit seppuku.

33:21.625 --> 33:23.333
I understand well…

33:25.500 --> 33:26.916
what you have in your hearts.

33:29.000 --> 33:30.458
The Kikuomi family…

33:31.916 --> 33:34.500
shall be restored by my hand at any cost.

33:35.458 --> 33:36.750
My Lord.

35:04.166 --> 35:05.541
You survived too.

35:13.750 --> 35:14.750
I have a favor to ask.

35:14.833 --> 35:16.000
Don't come any closer.

35:16.083 --> 35:16.916
What?

35:18.375 --> 35:22.125
No, wait! We don't want to fight anymore!

35:26.625 --> 35:29.000
We're going to abandon Kodoku!

35:29.083 --> 35:31.250
We just want you to join us!

35:32.666 --> 35:33.875
What are you saying?

35:36.416 --> 35:38.583
We were tricked into this. Weren't we?

35:38.666 --> 35:41.291
Yeah! That's right! We've been tricked!

35:42.541 --> 35:45.750
Some of the participants
are as strong as monsters.

35:45.833 --> 35:49.166
All the wooden tags
we grabbed were taken away!

35:50.416 --> 35:53.500
The 100,000 yen is all a lie!

35:56.833 --> 35:58.875
So, please. Join us.

36:00.375 --> 36:01.708
I'm begging you.

36:02.291 --> 36:04.333
Please, join us.

36:05.375 --> 36:07.500
You can't drop out
once you've joined the game.

36:07.583 --> 36:09.583
You'll be killed
if you break the rules.

36:09.666 --> 36:10.666
No.

36:11.250 --> 36:12.083
Even for them,

36:12.791 --> 36:15.625
it would be impossible
to attack so many of us.

36:15.708 --> 36:16.541
Wouldn't it?

36:19.833 --> 36:22.875
Why do we all have to kill each other?

36:27.375 --> 36:29.541
Just for this?

36:33.083 --> 36:36.916
All I wanted was some money.

36:39.458 --> 36:44.791
I only wanted to feed
my children enough food!

36:46.500 --> 36:48.083
Don't do it. Stop.

36:48.583 --> 36:49.958
They're watching us.

36:51.041 --> 36:52.333
I want to go home.

36:53.666 --> 36:55.250
Don't. Don't take it off.

36:55.333 --> 36:58.250
Don't do it. Don't do it! Stop!

37:25.916 --> 37:26.791
It's over.

37:37.583 --> 37:38.916
Are we done here?

38:16.458 --> 38:17.458
Don't take it off.

38:17.541 --> 38:20.625
-Home… I want to go home.
-Don't.

38:20.708 --> 38:22.291
Wait. Don't take it off! Wait!

38:23.708 --> 38:24.833
Don't!

38:26.500 --> 38:28.083
107

38:32.791 --> 38:33.791
It's okay.

38:34.375 --> 38:36.791
It's safe. Come on, take yours off too!

38:40.000 --> 38:41.541
Wait. Wait!

38:41.625 --> 38:42.916
-If you…
-Stop. Wait!

38:43.000 --> 38:44.708
Take yours off too--

39:05.375 --> 39:06.666
Why?

39:07.833 --> 39:08.916
It's so cruel.

40:03.458 --> 40:06.750
"Anyone who takes off their own
wooden tag will be punished accordingly."

40:06.833 --> 40:08.041
Is it clear to you now?

40:43.500 --> 40:45.416
To hell with you.

40:49.166 --> 40:53.041
What makes you think you're superior?

40:58.625 --> 41:00.916
You think you can do anything
to the samurai

41:03.000 --> 41:05.666
because we are useless now?

41:12.333 --> 41:13.375
What's wrong with you?

42:38.291 --> 42:39.333
Mr. Sakura, sir.

42:40.041 --> 42:41.333
What should we do?

42:43.750 --> 42:45.416
Report to the organizer.

42:46.500 --> 42:47.666
Understood.

42:56.458 --> 43:00.166
Kokushu the Manslayer has awakened.

43:39.916 --> 43:41.166
This…

43:43.958 --> 43:45.666
is who I used to be.

43:46.750 --> 43:47.583
What?

43:52.583 --> 43:55.333
All I knew was how to kill people.

44:25.583 --> 44:27.041
That wasn't enough.

44:28.083 --> 44:29.541
Not enough at all.

44:31.333 --> 44:32.208
There you go.

44:50.458 --> 44:53.458
117 REMAINING

48:55.958 --> 48:58.458
Subtitle translation by: Daisy Savage
